South African township music with upbeat jazz played by the band that features the leading young players on the Cape Town jazz scene. Long time Jonny Clegg sax-man, Shout, has a new band - infectious, sunny rhythms, catchy melodies, passionate solos&hellip;
Organised in collaboration with Wigan Jazz Festival.
&nbsp;

The blues-rock supergroup make their Festival debut. Their soul, funk and jam band roots, conjoins two southern USA music dynasties: vocalist, Cyrille Neville, and guitarist, Tyrone Vaughan, plus young blues guitar sensation, Bart Walker, and award winning rhythm team of Charlie Wootton and Yonrico Scott. White-hot musicianship with incendiary guitar duels and soulful vocals.
In a sensational double bill Mr Sipp (&ldquo;The Mississipi Blues Child&rdquo;) delivers his soulful and gritty music combining guitar excellence and vocal power, he cries out Mississippi blues with every note he plays.
&nbsp;

The German drummer brought his band to Edinburgh last winter and knocked everyone out. Terrific swing, great groove, loads of energy and detail, and a really tight, focused Quartet featuring the big tenor sax sound of Max von Mosch.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

'&rdquo;Sublime perfection&rdquo; (Maverick Magazine). Heather Macleod, Gina Rae and Cera Impala mix equal measures of sweetness and sass, grit and glamour, in their harmony vocal plus guitar band&nbsp; &ndash; imagine the Andrews Sisters with switchblades.
&nbsp;
